cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite both the software (this repository) and the accompanying publication."
title: "BRAVE: Bayesian Risk-aware Alloy discovery and Exploration (HTMDEC Campaign 2)"
abstract: >-
  Representative code, data, and manuscript for HTMDEC Campaign 2 — a Bayesian
  batch optimization framework for high-throughput alloy discovery in the
  Al–V–Cr–Mn–Fe–Co–Ni–Cu compositional space across five mechanical objectives.
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/mrinalinimulukutla/BRAVE"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Bayesian optimization
  - high-entropy alloys
  - alloy design
  - materials discovery
  - high-throughput
  - multi-objective optimization
  - Gaussian process
# Replace the placeholder DOI below with the Zenodo concept DOI after the first release.
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
